SmartSessionERC7739::_erc1271IsValidSignatureViaNestedEIP712
├── given a session key signature over the ERC-7739 TypedDataSign digest
│   ├── when the description is in implicit mode
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when the description is in explicit mode
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when the signature covers a different struct
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the hash is of another struct of the same type
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the signature covers a different app domain
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the signature covers a different account
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   └── when the signature is from a different key
│       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
├── given a struct with nested types
│   ├── when it is the EIP-712 example Mail struct
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when the type string lists the primary type first
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when the explicit-mode type string lists the dependencies first
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the signature covers the sorted TypedDataSign encoding
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   └── when the type string is not the app's type
│       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
├── given an explicit-mode contents name
│   ├── when the name differs from the primary type and the signature uses the name
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when the name differs from the primary type and the signature uses the primary type
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   └── when the name is not a valid contents name
│       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
├── given the session's allowed contents
│   ├── when the same struct uses a description the session did not enable
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the description is enabled under another app domain
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when each of two enabled types signs its own struct
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   └── when a struct is presented under the other enabled type
│       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
└── given fuzzed inputs
    ├── when the signature is arbitrary
    │   └── it never reverts and returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE or INVALID_SIGNATURE
    ├── when the appended data and trailer are arbitrary
    │   └── it never reverts and returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE or INVALID_SIGNATURE
    ├── when the envelope is correctly built
    │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
    ├── when one byte of the app domain, encodeData, description or trailer is flipped
    │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
    ├── when a struct of one type is presented under another enabled type
    │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
    ├── when the header is 0 to 80 bytes
    │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE only for a well-formed header of at least 64 bytes
    ├── when the hash is not the ERC-7739 probe
    │   └── it never returns 0x77390002
    └── when the hash is the ERC-7739 probe
        └── it returns 0x77390002